<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vatican Library</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1475">1475</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Vatican Apostolic Library</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Vatican Library is the library of the Holy See in Vatican City, formally established in 1475 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-sixtus-iv">Pope Sixtus IV</a>, building on the collection of Nicholas V. It holds one of the world's most important collections of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscripts</a>, including the Codex Vaticanus of the Bible. In 1623 much of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bibliotheca-palatina">Bibliotheca Palatina</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heidelberg">Heidelberg</a> was added to it as war booty.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vatican-library.jpg" alt="Vatican Library" width="320" height="380" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Melozzo da Forlì · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Melozzo_da_Forl%C3%AC_001.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
